{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in specifications. The policy gives forward motion priority in clear conditions, uses short directed turns for side/front obstacles, allows one rare backward escape only from a dedicated front-obstacle recovery state, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure state. Action states are one-shot through the motion plant, while specification states are total on uncontrollable events and bias back to forward exploration as soon as path_clear is observed.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion with two plant automata.",
    "Use one policy specification with perception and recovery helper states so each action state enables exactly one controllable action and obstacle handling always passes through recovery before exploration resumes."
  ],
  "G": [
